[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read the reports by tenant,
channel and form instead of by subject line, and it holds three problems. The queued parser fix
closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket. Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## What each one is

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant books 7 April
  and the invite says 4 July. Reports come from the app, by email, and from `booking-v2` forms.
- **`hint`**: `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type month first,
  and the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. Same symptom, different code: the
  parser fix does not touch it. Only form reports from `booking-v3` tenants.
- **`shift`**: the date moves by one day instead of flipping (Tuesday becomes Monday; Lisbon and
  Toronto get different days for one meeting). That is time zones, not date order. The desk spotted
  these by hand ([desk notes](/kb/incidents/4471)) and counts them where they are filed, under
  `parser`; this page counts them the same way and footnotes them.

## Why the table on #4471 says otherwise

The table on #4471 counts by cause as `causes.ts` knows it: the same counts as above, with the
one-day moves as a footnote instead of a ticket of their own, and `hint` with no ticket. Below is
that same table, unchanged:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## How to read reports next time

- Group by **tenant, channel and form**, not by subject or intake tag: intake guesses from the
  reporter's browser, and the tag differs from the problem on the counts above.
- A report that does not swap day and month is not this bug, whatever its subject says.
- The export repeats rows across pages; count by report id.

